@title Catalogue sync: delta pulls and batched writes for branch kiosks
@subtitle 10 commits, +2,033 / -292 lines. 1,204 of the added lines are test golden files.
@width wide

kpi Full resync (staging) | 9 min | was 41 min | good
kpi Reviewable change | +829 / -292 | excludes the 1,204 golden-file lines | neutral
kpi CI | 1 failure | known flake, also fails on main | bad

## What you are looking at

Kiosks used to re-fetch the catalogue. Now they pull only what changed since a saved `updated_since` cursor, and write it in batches of 500. That is commit `7be03d1` and it is the main thing. Everything else supports it: a refactor that splits fetch from apply, retry on 503, two bug fixes, a kiosk-client bump, test fixtures, a runbook, and one small feature (the "updated 3 min ago" banner) that product asked for and was not in the original scope.

Read in this order: `7be03d1`, then the batch size (`b26e9d4` and `0f7c3a1`), then the rest. The "Check first" section below lists what to verify.

## Why

- A full resync took 41 min on staging. It is 9 min with batched writes, and delta pulls mean most syncs never need a full one.
- The old parser broke on apostrophes and commas in titles. The golden files in `18cf6ab` cover this, including "Don't Look Now, and Other Stories".
- Records with MARC leader status `n` were being dropped (LIB-2214), found while testing this work.
- 503s from the catalogue needed a retry with backoff (`d813b42`).
- Product wanted kiosks to show how fresh the data is (`e5a7714`).

## What changed

### Sync pipeline (read carefully)
- `a41f9c2` **Split fetch from apply** (6 files, +212 / -188). Author says no behaviour change. Read it as moves, not edits. It is what keeps the next commit small.
- `7be03d1` **Delta pulls via `updated_since` cursor** (4 files, +341 / -52). The main change. Kiosks ask for records updated since a stored cursor instead of the whole catalogue.
- `c90e5aa` **Do not drop records with MARC leader `n` status** (2 files, +18 / -3). Found while testing. Ticket LIB-2214.
- `d813b42` **Retry with backoff on 503** (2 files, +37 / -6).

### Write batching (read carefully)
- `b26e9d4` **Batch writes in groups of 500** (2 files, +64 / -29). Full resync 41 min to 9 min on staging.
- `0f7c3a1` **Revert: batch size 2,000** (1 file, +1 / -1). 2,000 ran out of memory on the 1 GB kiosks at Eastgate and Pell Lane.

### Kiosk
- `3d2b8f0` **Bump kiosk-client to 4.12.1** (1 file, +2 / -2).
- `e5a7714` **Show "updated 3 min ago" banner** (3 files, +96 / -11). Product asked for this. Not in the original scope, and it can be split into its own PR if you prefer.

### Tests and docs (skim)
- `18cf6ab` **Golden files for 40 titles** (9 files, +1,204 / -0). Includes "Don't Look Now, and Other Stories". Apostrophes and commas broke the old parser.
- `9ad0e57` **Runbook for a stuck cursor** (1 file, +58 / -0).

data groups = group,commits,files,added,removed,review; Sync pipeline,4,14,608,249,Read carefully; Write batching,2,3,65,30,Read carefully; Kiosk,2,4,98,13,Read the banner; Golden files and docs,2,10,1262,0,Skim

table groups bar=added title="Where the lines are"

File counts are per commit, so a file touched by several commits is counted more than once.

## Check first

1. **The cursor in `7be03d1`.** Does it advance only after a batch has been applied? A cursor that moves before the apply completes would silently skip records. There is a runbook for a stuck cursor (`9ad0e57`), so this is a known way to go wrong.
2. **The batch size in `b26e9d4` and `0f7c3a1`.** The log lists the revert of 2,000 after the commit that sets 500. Please confirm the value in the tree is 500.
3. **Eastgate memory.** Eastgate is the pilot and is one of the 1 GB kiosks that ran out of memory at 2,000. The 41 to 9 min figure is from staging. Please confirm 500 has run on a 1 GB device.
4. **`d813b42` retry.** What are the backoff ceiling and the retry count, and does a retry resume from the cursor or restart the apply?
5. **`a41f9c2` refactor.** Diff it with move detection on. If it really is no behaviour change, the diff should be mostly relocated lines.
6. **`c90e5aa`.** Leader status `n` is "new" in MARC. Are other statuses (for example `d` for deleted) handled by delta pulls, and does a record deleted at the source disappear from kiosks?
7. **Golden files.** Spot-check three of the 40 titles, one of them the "Don't Look Now, and Other Stories" case.

Reviewer checklist:

- [ ] Cursor advances only after apply succeeds
- [ ] Batch size in the tree is 500
- [ ] 500 has run on a 1 GB kiosk
- [ ] Deleted and corrected records handled in delta pulls
- [ ] Retry resumes cleanly
- [ ] Banner reviewed or split out

## Risks

!! **The pilot is a small kiosk.** Eastgate is one of the 1 GB kiosks that ran out of memory at a batch size of 2,000. The 9 min resync was measured on staging, not on these kiosks.

!! **The failing integration test is in the code this PR changes.** `test_resume_after_partial_apply` fails about 1 run in 10 on main as well, so it is not new. But it covers resume after a partial apply, and this PR splits fetch from apply and adds batching. Run it many times before and after to be sure the failure rate has not moved.

! **Cursor and deletions.** A cursor-based pull gets changes, and whether it also gets removals depends on how the catalogue marks them. See check 6.

! **Rollback is slow, not hard.** Set the cursor back to null and run a full resync: about 9 min per kiosk, again from staging.

## Tests and CI

data ci = suite,passed,failed,skipped,duration; unit,"1,482",0,12,2m 14s; integration,214,1,3,9m 40s; kiosk-e2e,58,0,0,14m 02s

table ci

1,754 passed, 1 failed and 15 skipped across the three suites. The single failure is `test_resume_after_partial_apply`, which fails about 1 run in 10 on main as well.

## Rollout and rollback

step Pilot at Eastgate | Day 0
step Watch Eastgate: cursor movement, memory, resync time | Day 0 to 7
step Roll out to the other 11 branches | Day 7
step Rollback if needed: set the cursor to null, then full resync (about 9 min per kiosk) | Any time

## Deliberately left out

- **The flaky test.** `test_resume_after_partial_apply` is not fixed here. It fails on main already.
- **A bigger batch size.** 2,000 was tried and reverted, so nothing above 500 for small kiosks.
- **A wider rollout.** One branch first, the other 11 a week later.

